 now you know  made peace with everybody and i don't  have any hard feelings i i doubt there's  a lot of guys that have heart feelings  towards me  uh so it's just i try to compete i try  to win and then you know you know now  it's over it's we all had a good time  do you want to coach  be a gm  you know i'm not really sure what the  future brings honestly i've been  enjoying uh traveling my children have  three young kids and i'm enjoying being  home and traveling with them a lot and  i do some advising for the math at the  moment  to do other things uh learn about  business side and  uh you know we still have i have two  foundations one in germany one here in  the us so i stay busy  but you know we'll see what the future  brings i'm not a coach i would say  that's uh that's not my mentality to  stand there and motivate guys and hold  big speeches that was never my thing  even while i played  i was more the guy that led by example i  never wanted to stand in front of the  team and talk so i don't think that's in  my my dna but you know maybe some front  office stuff in in the future but well  we'll see what happens i think it's it's  a little too early for me i'm enjoying  my time with the family for now if i  said describe luka doncic to people  who've never seen him play  how would you describe it  i mean honestly he's  a complete package he's a big guard uh  he's  he's got everything in his game and  offensively that you would hope for i  mean he's he can break you down off the  dribble he's not the fastest guy he's a  big guy six nine big guy but uh you know  can can has has the skills as the the  strength  uh can go by anybody once he has you on  his butt on his shoulder he's so strong  he just can move anybody  and he's got the uh the big shot  mentality he's got the confidence to  take over in big moments so  he can post he worked on his floater  last couple years so now he's got the  in-between game  i mean honestly uh he is  as full of a package as a 23 year old as  i've seen because uh usually you know  how he reads the game how you reach the  pick-and-roll situation how he passed  the ball usually i think you develop  that more as you get more experience  this kid came in at 20 19 20 years old  and the way he saw the game was uh was  was something i've never seen in my  career so  we're we're so happy he's uh he's  playing for the mouse of course were you  ever called for an offensive foul when  you would do your little step back and  put your knee into somebody's groin  yeah not not not when i shot it but  sometimes i got it when i try to create  space and somebody was really on me and  i'd really try to put my shoulder down  and create  that little bit of you know separation  that i needed i think  especially later in my career when guys  knew that i was coming i didn't really i  couldn't really drive uh and i did so  they were really up on my shoulder and  then when i did try to lower it a little  bit i think that's when i got some  offense foul but once i got the little  separation and i was leaning back  i don't think i ever got uh got that  call as much test fell yeah but you were  you were using your leg as a weapon dirk  i mean a little bit but like i said that  you first you first create the  separation with backing somebody down  and then once you take a step back you  know it's not like i  i bumped and then immediately shot i did  step back from from a little from one  felt to the other from the right leg to  the left and that is already creating  enough separation  to raise the the knee up so i never  really need anybody uh in the groin or  in other areas during that shot that  never really happened has mark cuban  ever been the best shooter on the team  uh never uh he i think in his his his  mind he believes he was uh but  honestly he's uh he played a little bit  obviously uh as a hobby and he's got a  little stroke but it's it's a super  super slow slow release  uh  but uh you know he was just a super fan  when we first when he bought the team we  used to play one-on-one in shooting  games after practice all the time and  that's the kind of relationship we had  and so he's he's been sort of a mentor  and  uh and obviously a good friend of mine  for for a long long time so i do i do  owe him a lot uh thanks for opening up  the scrapbook we appreciate you uh  telling stories there dirk thank you  very much yeah no thank you guys for  having me take care that's dirk nowitzki


